You may use hex codes instead of name colors for CSS coloring.

CSS fonts can be styled with color, font weight, font size, and font family.

REM is the best for sizing elements because it refers to the root, offering consistency.
Font family is the font type. You should put a generic font (serif/sans serif) behind a comma and the font type as backup.

Margin, padding, and border styling exists for CSS box models.

<div></div> is known as the content division element and is used to create artificial boxes. Any elements put between the opening and closing tags are grouped into a box.